array again. Anything else is a list. \code{simplify = "none"} makes every
array a list.

With \code{datetimes = "keep"}, date-times are returned as RFC 3339 text
instead (\code{"1979-05-27T07:32:00Z"}, a zero offset written \code{Z}, the fraction
in 0, 3, 6 or 9 digits). Fractions past nanoseconds are truncated, as
TOML requires; a \code{POSIXct} holds microseconds.

